[size=5][b]Debug Draw[/b][/size]
[size=3]Draw lines, shapes, text and graphs in the world from your mod, and see what the engine sees: collision, navmesh and trigger volumes.[/size]

[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Debug Draw is a resource for mod authors. It turns the game's own debug renderer back on and hands it to redscript and Cyber Engine Tweaks, so one line of script puts a line, box, sphere, arrow, label or live graph in the world. Use it to see raycasts, AI targets, spawn radii, paths, vehicle forces, or anything else your mod is doing, right where it happens.

It also works on its own: switch on the world overlays from its settings page to see the collision, navmesh and trigger volumes around V, no scripting needed.

It is a native C++ RED4ext plugin. Shapes go straight to the engine's debug renderer, not through ink widgets or spawned entities, so it keeps up with tens of thousands of lines a frame. (In engine terms: every camera normally gets a NullDebugDrawer that throws everything away. This hands it a real one.)

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Shapes:[/b] lines, paths, arrows, boxes, oriented boxes, spheres, circles, discs, capsules, cylinders, cones, axes gizmos, triangles and polygons, as wireframes or filled (with transparency), with an optional line thickness.
[*][b]Text and data:[/b] world text with a readable outline, screen text, labels that follow entities, and rolling graphs (Plot) for values that change every frame.
[*][b]Helpers:[/b] Raycast and Trace draw a ray you cast and where it hit; Bounds and Velocity draw an entity's bounding box and velocity arrow; Heat turns a value into a blue-to-red colour.
[*][b]Timing and ownership:[/b] draw for one frame or for N seconds; every shape belongs to a channel, so Clear only removes your own.
[*][b]Following things:[/b] PushTransform and PushEntity put shapes in a local space; shapes queued under an entity stay on it as it moves.
[*][b]Seeing it clearly:[/b] overlay mode draws through walls, X-ray shows a channel's hidden shapes faintly, and Dim darkens the scene so debug shapes stand out.
[*][b]World overlays:[/b] wireframes of the physics shapes (static in pale green, moving in orange), the navmesh NPCs walk on, and trigger volumes. Turn them on around V from the settings page, or draw them around any point from script. Moving bodies are updated every frame, so their wireframes stay on the cars and NPCs.
[*][b]Materials and custom shaders:[/b] built-in looks (lit, grid, hologram, distance fade, pulse, scanlines, stripes), material parameters you can change from script, and your own HLSL shaders through the included compiler. Shaders reload in game without a restart.
[*][b]Settings[/b] (with Mod Settings): show or hide everything any mod draws, text size, label distance, dim strength, and the world overlays.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Quick start[/b][/size]
From redscript:
[code]
DebugDraw.Line(a, b, DebugDraw.Rgba(255, 64, 0), 5.0);           // for 5 seconds
DebugDraw.Sphere(center, 2.0, DebugDraw.Rgba(0, 128, 255));        // this frame
DebugDraw.Label(npc, "searching", DebugDraw.Rgba(255, 255, 255), 0.0, n"my_mod");
DebugDraw.Plot("speed", speed);
DebugDrawOverlays.ShowCollision(GetPlayer(game).GetWorldPosition(), 15.0);
[/code]
From a CET mod or the CET console, the same functions work:
[code]
DebugDraw.Sphere(Vector4.new(p.x, p.y, p.z + 2.5, 1), 0.5, DebugDraw.Rgba(255, 128, 0, 0))
[/code]
The full API, a cookbook of common uses, and the shader guide are in the readme included in the download.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
Install with a mod manager, or by hand: extract the archive into the game folder (the one with bin, archive and r6), so the files land in red4ext/plugins/debug_draw and archive/pc/mod.

To check it works: with Mod Settings installed, open Mod Settings from the pause menu and turn on Debug Draw > World overlays > Show overlays around V, and the collision and navmesh around V should appear. Without it, look in red4ext/logs for a debug_draw log: a working install logs "Added the debug render nodes to the main render graph" when a save loads.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]RED4ext[/b] 1.31.0 or newer
[*][b]Redscript[/b] 0.5.32 or newer
[*][b]Mod Settings[/b] (optional) for the settings page; without it the defaults apply
[*][b]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/b] (optional) to draw from CET
[/list]
Built for Cyberpunk 2077 2.5 (executable 3.0.88). Engine functions are found by hash, so other versions may work; if one is not found, the log says so and the mod draws nothing, while scripts that call it still compile and run.

[size=4][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Use your own channel name (for example n"my_mod") so your shapes, Clear calls, materials and X-ray settings never touch another mod's.
[*]Debug shapes are drawn after the game's lighting: they never get its shadows or lights. The lit, grid and hologram materials do their own shading.
[*]Players can hide all debug drawing and change text size from the settings page, so you can leave your debug drawing in and let them switch it off.
[/list]

